#: buildVars.py:15
msgid "freeRadio"
msgstr "freeRadio"

#: buildVars.py:19
msgid ""
"FreeRadio is an internet radio, podcast, and audio-book add-on for NVDA that "
"provides seamless access to thousands of internet radio stations via the "
"Radio Browser open directory, RSS/Atom podcast feeds, and the GETEM digital "
"library for the visually impaired. It features a fully accessible station "
"browser with search, country filter, favourites management, and per-station, "
"per-podcast, and per-audio-book audio profiles. Podcast episodes and audio "
"book chapters resume automatically from where you left off, with adjustable "
"pitch-preserving playback speed. Playback is handled by a prioritised "
"backend chain (BASS, VLC, PotPlayer, Windows Media Player) with support for "
"volume control, audio effects, output device selection, and simultaneous "
"audio mirroring to a second device. Additional features include instant and "
"scheduled recording, time-shift rewind of live radio, sleep and alarm "
"timers, automatic ICY metadata announcements, Shazam-based music "
"recognition, and a liked-songs log with lyrics lookup. All controls and "
"shortcuts are designed for NVDA accessibility."
msgstr ""
"FreeRadio es un complemento de radio por Internet, podcast, y audiolibro "
"para NVDA que proporciona un acceso continuo a miles de estaciones a través "
"del directorio abierto de Radio Browser, Fuentes de podcast RSS/Atom y La "
"biblioteca digital GETEM para personas con discapacidad visual. Cuenta con "
"un navegador de estaciones totalmente accesible con búsqueda, filtro de "
"países, administración de favoritos y perfiles de audio por estación, por "
"podcast y por audiolibro. Los episodios de podcasts y los capítulos de "
"audiolibros se reanudan automáticamente desde donde los dejaste, con una "
"velocidad de reproducción ajustable que conserva el tono. La reproducción es "
"manejada por una cadena de backend priorizada (BASS, VLC, PotPlayer, Windows "
"Media Player) con soporte para control de volumen, efectos de audio, "
"selección de dispositivo de salida y la puesta en espejo de audio simultánea "
"en un segundo dispositivo. Las características adicionales incluyen "
"grabación instantánea y programada, desplazamiento temporal rebobinar radio "
"en directo, temporizadores de apagado y alarma, anuncios automáticos de "
"metadatos ICY, reconocimiento de música basado en Shazam y un registro de "
"canciones favoritas con búsqueda de letras. Todos los controles y atajos "
"están diseñados para la accesibilidad de NVDA."

#: buildVars.py:26
msgid ""
"\n"
"**Security**\n"
"- Certificate verification for streaming connections (live playback, "
"recording, and time-shift) is now enabled by default, closing a gap where "
"every station's stream could previously be intercepted or substituted "
"without warning. Stations with known broken/expired certificates "
"automatically fall back to an unverified connection so they keep working — "
"nothing else changes for those stations, and only they pay a small extra "
"delay the first time they're opened each session.\n"
"**Fixed**\n"
"- **Audio books:** Fixed a rare timing issue where, right as one chapter "
"finished and the next was about to start automatically, playback could "
"occasionally jump backward to an already-heard chapter instead of continuing "
"forward. Most noticeable during long unattended listening sessions.\n"
"- **Scheduled recordings:** Recurring recordings now recover much more "
"reliably after your PC wakes from sleep or when NVDA was closed for a "
"while:\n"
"  - A missed recurring recording on a multi-day schedule (e.g. Mon/Wed/Fri) "
"no longer skips ahead by a full week — it correctly finds the next eligible "
"day.\n"
"  - Old, incorrectly saved schedule dates from earlier versions are "
"automatically fixed on load — no need to recreate them.\n"
"  - If a recording's start was delayed (e.g. by sleep), it now records only "
"the time actually remaining in its original window, instead of starting a "
"full-length recording late.\n"
"  - Schedule data is now saved more safely, preventing rare cases of a "
"damaged or incomplete schedule file.\n"
"  - While a scheduled recording is in progress, Windows is prevented from "
"going into idle sleep automatically.\n"
"**Added**\n"
"- New keyboard shortcuts for quick access:\n"
"  - `Ctrl+Windows+L` — jumps straight to the Audio Books tab (focus on your "
"library).\n"
"  - `Ctrl+Windows+O` — jumps straight to the Podcasts tab (focus on your "
"subscriptions).\n"
"  - Both open the FreeRadio window if it's closed, or bring it to the front "
"if it's already open.\n"
"- More audio profile options when saving a profile for a podcast or "
"audiobook: **Volume and playback speed**, **Effects and playback speed**, "
"and **Playback speed only**, alongside the existing Volume only / Effects "
"only / Volume and effects / Volume, effects, and playback speed choices.\n"
"- The **Save Audio Profile for This Podcast** and **Clear Audio Profile** "
"commands are now also available from the episode context menu, so you don't "
"need to switch back to the podcast list to reach them. They still apply to "
"the whole podcast, not to a single episode.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"**Seguridad**\n"
"- La verificación de certificados para conexiones de transmisión "
"(reproducción en directo, grabación y desplazamiento temporal) ahora está "
"habilitada de manera predeterminada, cerrando una brecha donde antes la "
"transmisión de cada estación podía ser interceptada o sustituida sin previo "
"aviso. Las estaciones con certificados rotos o caducados conocidos "
"automáticamente recurren a una conexión no verificada para que sigan "
"funcionando; nada más cambia para esas estaciones, y solo pagan un pequeño "
"retraso adicional la primera vez que se abren en cada sesión.\n"
"**Fijo**\n"
"- **Audiolibros:** Se solucionó un problema poco común de sincronización "
"donde, justo cuando un capítulo terminaba y el siguiente estaba a punto de "
"comenzar automáticamente, la reproducción ocasionalmente podía saltar hacia "
"atrás a un capítulo ya escuchado en lugar de continuar hacia adelante. Se "
"nota más durante largas sesiones de escucha sin supervisión.\n"
"- **Grabaciones programadas:** Las grabaciones recurrentes ahora se "
"recuperan de manera mucho más confiable después de que tu PC sale del modo "
"de suspensión o cuando NVDA estuvo cerrado por un tiempo:\n"
"  - Una grabación recurrente perdida en un programa de varios días (por "
"ejemplo, lunes, miércoles y viernes) ya no avanza una semana completa; "
"encuentra correctamente el siguiente día elegible.\n"
"  - Las fechas de programación antiguas y guardadas incorrectamente de "
"versiones anteriores se corrigen automáticamente al cargar, sin necesidad de "
"volver a crearlas.\n"
"  - Si el inicio de una grabación se retrasó (por ejemplo, por el modo de "
"suspensión), ahora registra solo el tiempo que realmente queda en su ventana "
"original, en lugar de iniciar tarde una grabación completa.\n"
"  - Los datos del programa ahora se guardan de forma más segura.evitando "
"casos raros de un archivo de programación dañado o incompleto.\n"
"  - Mientras se realiza una grabación programada, se evita que Windows entre "
"en suspensión automáticamente.\n"
"**Añadido**\n"
"- Nuevos atajos de teclado para un acceso rápido:\n"
"  - `Ctrl+Windows+L`: salta directamente a la pestaña Audiolibros "
"(enfocándose en su biblioteca).\n"
"  - `Ctrl+Windows+O`: salta directamente a la pestaña Podcasts (enfocándose "
"en sus suscripciones).\n"
"  - Ambos abren la ventana de FreeRadio si está cerrada, o la llevan al "
"frente si ya está abierta.\n"
"- Más opciones de perfil de audio al guardar un perfil para un podcast o "
"audiolibro: **Volumen y velocidad de reproducción**, **Efectos y velocidad "
"de reproducción** y **Solo velocidad de reproducción**, junto con las "
"opciones existentes Solo volumen/Solo efectos/Volumen y efectos/Volumen, "
"efectos y velocidad de reproducción.\n"
"- Las órdenes **Guardar perfil de audio para este podcast** y **Borrar "
"perfil de audio** ahora también están disponibles en el menú contextual del "
"episodio, por lo que no es necesario volver a la lista de podcasts para "
"acceder a ellos. Todavía se aplican a todo el podcast, no a un solo "
"episodio.\n"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "\n"
#~ "## scheduled recording fixes\n"
#~ "**Fixed**\n"
#~ "- Recurring scheduled recordings would only fire once and never repeat "
#~ "correctly.\n"
#~ "  - Fixed a thread-safety race where the scheduler loop's per-second "
#~ "cleanup of the schedule list could silently drop a freshly re-queued "
#~ "recurring recording before it was ever saved or checked.\n"
#~ "  - Fixed date calculation for recurring schedules: the next occurrence "
#~ "was always computed a full week ahead before checking active days, so a "
#~ "schedule set to record every day (e.g. daily at 09:00) actually only re-"
#~ "fired once a week on the original weekday. It now correctly schedules the "
#~ "very next matching day.\n"
#~ "**Note**\n"
#~ "- Existing entries in `freeradio_schedules.json` created before this fix "
#~ "may still hold a `start_time` computed by the old logic (a week ahead). "
#~ "Recreate those schedules, or manually correct their `start_time`, to get "
#~ "correct daily firing going forward.\n"
#~ "## Fixes for chapter Auto-advance and playback speed\n"
#~ "**Bug Fix — Audio Book Chapter Auto-Advance Stopped When FreeRadio Window "
#~ "Was Closed**\n"
#~ "- Fixed an issue where an audio book would correctly move to its next "
#~ "chapter when it finished playing while the FreeRadio window was open on "
#~ "the Audio Books tab, but silently stopped at the end of a chapter instead "
#~ "of advancing if the window was closed or hidden.\n"
#~ "- Chapter auto-advance no longer depends on the FreeRadio dialog being "
#~ "open: it now runs independently in the background, using the finished "
#~ "chapter's own book/part information to look up the next chapter and start "
#~ "it directly.\n"
#~ "- Progress tracking (which chapter/part you're on) is now saved correctly "
#~ "even while advancing in the background.\n"
#~ "- When the FreeRadio window is reopened, its \"now playing\" state (used "
#~ "by F3/F4 chapter/book navigation) is refreshed from the player, so it "
#~ "correctly reflects a book that kept advancing while the window was "
#~ "closed.\n"
#~ "**Bug Fix — Playback Speed Leaking Between Audio Books/Podcasts**\n"
#~ "- Fixed an issue where saving an audio profile with a sped-up playback "
#~ "rate (e.g. 1.4x) for one book, then switching to another book with no "
#~ "saved profile, would leave the second book playing at the first book's "
#~ "speed instead of normal speed.\n"
#~ "- Playback speed now follows the same rule already used for volume/"
#~ "effects/EQ: if the book or podcast being played has a saved profile with "
#~ "a speed, that speed is applied; otherwise, speed resets to normal (1.0x) "
#~ "rather than carrying over from whatever was played previously.\n"
#~ "- Arabic localization update\n"
#~ "## startup resume fixes\n"
#~ "**Bug Fix — Audio Profile Not Applied on Startup Resume**\n"
#~ "- Fixed an issue where a saved audio profile (volume/effects/EQ/speed) "
#~ "for a podcast or audio book was applied correctly when starting playback "
#~ "from the dialog, but was ignored when the station resumed automatically "
#~ "on NVDA startup.\n"
#~ "- Playing a podcast episode now also records which feed it belongs to; "
#~ "playing an audio book chapter already recorded which book it belongs to.\n"
#~ "- On startup resume:\n"
#~ "  - For audio books, the saved book profile is now looked up and applied "
#~ "together with the rebuilt playback URL.\n"
#~ "  - For podcast episodes, the subscribed feed is looked up independently "
#~ "(without needing the dialog open) and its saved profile, if any, is "
#~ "applied the same way.\n"
#~ "- As a result, resumed playback on NVDA startup now respects the same "
#~ "volume, effects, EQ, and playback speed settings as playback started "
#~ "manually from the dialog.\n"
#~ "## Recording tab rearrangements and audio profiles for podcasts and audio "
#~ "books\n"
#~ "**Recording Tab**\n"
#~ "- Removed the \"Edit\" and \"Remove\" buttons; their functionality moved "
#~ "into the list's context menu (Applications key / Shift+F10).\n"
#~ "- Delete / Shift+Delete now removes the selected schedule directly.\n"
#~ "- Default mode is now \"Record only\".\n"
#~ "- After removing a schedule, the next item in the list (or the previous "
#~ "one, if it was the last) is automatically selected.\n"
#~ "**Podcast and Audio Book Tabs**\n"
#~ "- F3 / F4 / Shift+F3 / Shift+F4 now also move keyboard focus to the "
#~ "relevant list (previously they only changed the selection).\n"
#~ "- On the Audio Book tab, since there's no separate list item for "
#~ "chapters, changing chapters moves focus to the book's row in the library "
